{"id":30874550830,"name":"Run api tests","node_id":"WFR_kwLOA_1uaM8AAAAHMERCLg","head_branch":"claude/uganda-9-datavalueset-flushmode","head_sha":"a1bc7b3f05660de3dab38104f7c83d772c002de0","path":".github/workflows/run-api-tests.yml","run_number":51683,"run_attempt":1,"event":"pull_request","display_title":"perf: suppress auto-flush over the dataValueSets import's read-only span","status":"completed","conclusion":"success","workflow_id":5591308,"check_suite_id":83721809493,"check_suite_node_id":"CS_kwDOA_1uaM8AAAATfjVuVQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dhis2/dhis2-core/actions/runs/30874550830","html_url":"https://github.com/dhis2/dhis2-core/actions/runs/30874550830","created_at":"2026-08-04T03:22:09Z","updated_at":"2026-08-04T03:34:36Z","run_started_at":"2026-08-04T03:22:09Z","jobs_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dhis2/dhis2-core/actions/runs/30874550830/jobs","logs_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dhis2/dhis2-core/actions/runs/30874550830/logs","check_suite_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dhis2/dhis2-core/check-suites/83721809493","artifacts_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dhis2/dhis2-core/actions/runs/30874550830/artifacts","cancel_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dhis2/dhis2-core/actions/runs/30874550830/cancel","rerun_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dhis2/dhis2-core/actions/runs/30874550830/rerun","head_commit":{"message":"perf: suppress auto-flush over the dataValueSets import's read-only span\n\nA dataValueSets import runs as one transaction with one Hibernate session and\nloads a large read-only metadata graph into the persistence context. Under the\ndefault FlushModeType.AUTO every query it issues makes Hibernate dirty-check\nthat entire context first, and the context grows for the whole import, so the\ncost per value rises with the values already processed - quadratic CPU on the\nread path.\n\nThe Uganda Glowroot traces measured this as 28.3 s of CPU in a 29.7 s request\n(1.33 s of JDBC, zero blocked time), with the same query costing 9-20x more at\nthe end of a request than at the start.\n\nHibernate does the dirty check even when it then decides no flush is needed:\nDefaultAutoFlushEventListener.onAutoFlush calls flushEverythingToExecutions\nbefore testing flushIsReallyNeeded, and only counts a flush inside the \"really\nneeded\" branch. So the work is invisible in Statistics.getFlushCount(), which\nreports zero flushes for these imports.\n\nMetadata resolution, cache preheating and validation only read, so suppress the\nflush across that span and restore the previous mode before the first write.\nNothing in the window writes through Hibernate: data values go through a\nraw-JDBC BatchHandler, and missing periods are created in a stateless session\n(the DHIS2-7539 FK-ordering fix). The two Hibernate writes in the import -\nFileResource updates and handleComplete's CompleteDataSetRegistration - are\nboth outside it; handleComplete is the one place where the auto-flush is\nload-bearing, which is why the flush mode is not set session-wide.\n\nMeasured on 2.42.5.1-ug-ereg-custom with the L2 cache off, importing 166 values\nagainst 2000 restricted org units:\n\n  dirty-check passes  665,686 -\u003e 2,015   (330x fewer)\n  import wall-clock     3,015 ms -\u003e 553 ms (5.5x faster)\n  values imported         166 -\u003e 166     (identical)\n  auto-flush events        91 -\u003e  91     (identical - no query removed)\n\nAdds DataValueSetImportAutoFlushTest, which counts FlushEntityEvents and fails\non the unfixed code.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 \u003cnoreply@anthropic.com\u003e","author":{"name":"Stian Sandvold","email":"stian@dhis2.org"},"id":"a1bc7b3f05660de3dab38104f7c83d772c002de0","tree_id":"f1910bfbc3a662e82a4e91fd194cc987835343c7","timestamp":"2026-08-03T23:58:00Z","committer":{"name":"Stian Sandvold","email":"stian@dhis2.org"}},"workflow_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dhis2/dhis2-core/actions/workflows/5591308","repository":{"id":66940520,"node_id":"MDEwOlJlcG9zaXRvcnk2Njk0MDUyMA==",